      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62931a5795016b0b83072861|full_name} I'm in the camp of 'not far enough'. As an accessibility option alone, the distance of 3rd person camera view helps compensate for the lack of FOV avaliable. FOV 100 is too low for my comfort, but with the 3rd person distance so far, that FOV is finally bearable. No more is my head splitting from playing desktop mode.\n\nWhen this was first implemented I immediately thought of the privacy concerns, but in practice of using it I'm not sure something like this really makes sense in the spirit of the game. For the immersion sense of the VR userbase, this seems more distracting than it's worth. To me this moreso pushes into the 'annoying' side than anything, which could be resolved with user moderation.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
